A||N||5||AgaricX||18's vs 17's||||1||
Z||000000||AgaricX||12-16-2001||04:38 PM||||Are there any issues in putting 18" rims on the rear and 17" rims on the front?  Does it adversely affect performance?  I like the larger weheel in the rear look personally, but want to make sure it wont screw up something.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/AgaricX.jpg">  <BR>'85 SE 3800SC 5 Spd<BR>I WANT A FASTBACK!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||avengador1||12-16-2001||04:57 PM||||I don't think it should affect anything, especially if you get the right size tires. In this case you would be running a plus 2 size in the front and a plus 3 size in the rear. The only thing to be concerned about is the plus 3 size will have a shorter sidewall and the wheel will be more prone to be damaged by potholes,etc. Check out <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tirerack.com</A>  to see how they would look. The plus sizes are to keep the outside circumference as close to stock as possible.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||12-16-2001||06:49 PM||||Chris Moore has been running 18s on the rear and 17s in front on his blue Northstar for a couple years now, with no probs.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">                 <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A> *<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa1/showdates.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Events 2002</A> *<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tarheel Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||12-16-2001||11:02 PM||||Stiffens up the rear a bit more even, go for it!<P>Don't be afraid to get slightly larger than stock rooling rubber in the back, speedo nazis be damned.  245/40/18 rear on an 18x8 wheel will be nice. (with say 215/45/17 front)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||AgaricX||12-17-2001||03:20 AM||||So, what's the max size I can pull off having with 18's rear/ 17's front?  I don't plan on dropping the car... maybe 1.5" awhile from now, but not for quite awhile.  I'm REALLY liking your 18's BTW!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/AgaricX.jpg">  <BR>'85 SE 3800SC 5 Spd<BR>I WANT A FASTBACK!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||12-17-2001||04:32 AM||||You mean these?  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/northstar/2/10-rear4.jpg">   <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Thanks for the compliments, I love 'em too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Note they're just set in the wells, no suspension there yet. Have to build it.<P>For those (18x10, 265/35/18) I'm naturally having to go coilover, and my spherical rod-end suspension links are going to give me a bit (+-about20mm) of track ajustment.  I *think* they'll barely fit!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  This is also in an 88, which I belive can take slightly larger wheels? (not sure if the wheelwells are actually any different or not though.)<P>I think you can stuff at least 18x9s (with 255/40/18 or 255-35/18) in the rear with coilovers on a 87-84.  LT1 Chop Top has this on his red 88 GT.<P>You can certinly do 18x8" rear with the same 255/40(or35)/18 rubber with no problems.<P>No need to go larger than 7" fronts with 215/45/17. my 18s are actually 18x7.5" with 225/40/18 front, maybe on the edge of being TOO big.  Our cars are so nimble that they turn HARD on very little front rubber, and past a certin point, all you are doing is making the car hard to turn.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AgaricX:<BR><B>So, what's the max size I can pull off having with 18's rear/ 17's front?  I don't plan on dropping the car... maybe 1.5" awhile from now, but not for quite awhile.  I'm REALLY liking your 18's BTW!!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
